@participant11, can we reopen this?

I'm having the same problem. I must access data from a self-hosted [Apache Ozone](https://ozone.apache.org/docs/1.0.0/interface/s3.html) instance with self-signed certificates via the S3 protocol. I can use Python's boto3 library to provide the trusted certificates through the `verify` argument. I would expect a similar mechanism from DuckDB.

The httpfs extension seems to be built around [cpp-httplib](https://github.com/yhirose/cpp-httplib). Looking at the [documentation](https://github.com/yhirose/cpp-httplib), it seems possible to speficy your own CA bundle:

``` 
// Use your CA bundle
cli.set_ca_cert_path("./ca-bundle.crt");
```

I image anyone using DuckDB on top of a self-hosted blob store with self-signed certificates is affected by this problem.
